# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses f4c9d13865f3, 2026-10-19
just_lives_well	two	live well	P5	the just soul performs its function of living excellently	the just man fares well, i.e. is blessed and prosperous
unjust_lives_ill	two	lives ill	P5	the unjust soul performs its function of living badly	the unjust man fares badly, i.e. is wretched
life_end	one
just_excellent	one
# "excellence" in S8/S10 is the soul's excellence at its work, while S12 calls moral justice that excellence; but S12 is a single asserted premise, so I left this claim as one sense.
